<speak>Your objective is to reduce your exposure to Asian equities and keep funds available for your business needs. Meridian Asia Equity Fund can fall in value when Asian equity markets weaken or its portfolio companies report disappointing results. Market volatility can also affect what you receive when you reduce the holding. You may lose some or even all of the capital you invested in the fund. Do you understand how those market movements and company results can affect the fund's value and what you receive?</speak>